fc-b17e-3f08e92d5d7d","relation":"discovered_from","target_id":"d48d-76bd-3d31-47ea"}],"description":"## Context / Problem\n\nTicket `d48d-76bd-3d31-47ea` added a fifth validity sub-question (`harm_reachable`) to the\nrebar-janitor Verification phase and updated the normative scoring formula in\n`examples/agent-skills/rebar-janitor/phases/verification.md` to read \"graded fraction of the 5\nbinary sub-answers\". Two *secondary prose glosses* elsewhere in the same file still say four, so\nthe file is internally inconsistent about the count:\n\n- the drop-floor parenthetical at line 152: `(low-confidence — <~3-of-4 sub-answers affirm it)`\n- the known-fine registry aside at line 191: `it is NOT one of the four validity sub-questions`\n\nNeither is the normative rule (the formula bullet is), so nothing computes from them — but a reader\ncounting sub-questions gets contradictory answers from the same document.\n\n## Approach\n\nUpdate both glosses to agree with the normative formula. Both replacements are stated verbatim\nbelow; there is no implementer discretion.\n\n1. **Drop-floor parenthetical (line 152).** The floor is `validity < 0.75`. Over 5 sub-answers,\n   4-of-5 = 0.80 **survives** and 3-of-5 = 0.60 **drops**, so the survive/drop boundary is\n   **4-of-5**, not a literal denominator swap to `3-of-5` (which would misdescribe the floor).\n   Replace the parenthetical with exactly:\n   `(low-confidence — <4-of-5 sub-answers affirm it)`\n2. **Known-fine aside (line 191).** Replace `four validity sub-questions` with\n   `five validity sub-questions`. No other wording on that line changes.\n\nLine 140 (`**impact** = mean of four terms`) is a *different* count — the four impact terms — and\nis deliberately left alone.\n\nNo rule, threshold, or behavior changes: the normative arithmetic already reads 5.\n\n## Scope\n\n- `examples/agent-skills/rebar-janitor/phases/verification.md` — the drop-floor parenthetical in the\n  `## The floors` code block and the `matches_known_fine` aside in the `## Known-fine registry`\n  section. Nothing else in the file or repo changes.\n\n## Testing\n\nDocumentation-only prose edit with no executable path, schema, or test fixture; verification is\ntextual (see Acceptance Criteria). The acceptance criteria assert both the *removal* of the stale\ntext and the *presence* of the exact replacement text, so a wrong replacement cannot pass.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] The drop-floor gloss no longer says `3-of-4`; checked by\n      `grep -n '3-of-4' examples/agent-skills/rebar-janitor/phases/verification.md` exiting non-zero.\n- [ ] The drop-floor gloss now reads the correct boundary; checked by\n      `grep -nF '<4-of-5 sub-answers affirm it' examples/agent-skills/rebar-janitor/phases/verification.md`\n      exiting zero with exactly one match, on the `validity < 0.75` line of the `## The floors` block.\n- [ ] No `3-of-5` gloss is introduced; checked by\n      `grep -n '3-of-5' examples/agent-skills/rebar-janitor/phases/verification.md` exiting non-zero.\n- [ ] The known-fine aside no longer says `four validity sub-questions`; checked by\n      `grep -n 'four validity sub-questions' examples/agent-skills/rebar-janitor/phases/verification.md`\n      exiting non-zero, and now says the five form; checked by\n      `grep -nF 'five validity' examples/agent-skills/rebar-janitor/phases/verification.md` exiting zero.\n- [ ] No count-of-four reference to the validity sub-question set survives in the file; checked by\n      `grep -nE 'the 4 (binary )?sub|four validity' examples/agent-skills/rebar-janitor/phases/verification.md`\n      exiting non-zero.\n- [ ] The unrelated `mean of four terms` impact gloss is untouched; checked by\n      `grep -nF 'mean of four terms' examples/agent-skills/rebar-janitor/phases/verification.md`\n      exiting zero.\n- [ ] The change is self-contained: the normative `5 binary sub-answers` formula bullet is already\n      present in the file at edit time (`grep -nF '5 binary sub-answers'` exits zero), so this\n      ticket depends on no unlanded work.\n- [ ] `make lint` exits 0 with the repo venv on PATH.","env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","file_impact":[{"path":"examples/agent-skills/rebar-janitor/phases/verification.md","reason":"align the drop-floor and known-fine count-of-four glosses with the five-sub-question formula"}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"last_status_env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","managed_refs":[],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":null,"parent_status_uuid":"e50105a6-e6c1-43db-9a78-b4621f41972e","plan_review_phase":"execution","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":2,"reverts":[],"status":"in_progress","tags":["janitor"],"ticket_id":"1d7a-9f76-139b-4259","ticket_type":"task","title":"Align the two count-of-four prose glosses in rebar-janitor verification.md","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["e37f4b6d-678e-4751-abb5-c4a6325e6295","ff04d1dc-8565-4faf-b0e9-dfd15928ae02","0d3e6d38-60cd-4afc-b17e-3f08e92d5d7d","c98a44f7-832e-474a-9407-f37153279c1c","188e6e0d-4ecd-4811-ba86-ae7400ea0be6","e50105a6-e6c1-43db-9a78-b4621f41972e","1ff71c3a-6f68-4941-91a1-cced1db55a75"]},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1786096541185258002,"uuid":"9e9ed76d-dc9f-4aa7-8d73-2a313694acac"}